text:
C# got Tuple only in version 7.0 which was released in 2017, if you don&#x27;t know; while TryParse has been there since 1.0 in 2002. And I&#x27;d still prefer to have e.g.<p><pre><code>    if ([double val, bool ok] = double.TryParse(&quot;5.x5&quot;); ok) {
        Console.WriteLine(val);
    } else {
        Console.WriteLine(&quot;err&quot;);
    }
</code></pre>
Of course, having &quot;var&quot; there would be even nicer.
